    },
    {
      "text": "Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "VariAx 2 Distal Ulna Plating System provides you with a comprehensive range of anatomic plating options that work with a common instrument and screw platform",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Plates utilize SmartLock technology which permits polyaxial screw placement",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "You can angle locking screws up to 15˚in each direction for a total range of 30˚ providing you with the flexibility to position screws based on the patient, not a plate’s pre-existing design",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423223/images/858c584b-2bed-4b14-a4db-25cdcda32985_screenshot_2025-03-27_at_10.24.33_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The VariAx 2 Distal Ulnar System is indicated for the treatment of:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Malunions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The DU Hook Plate may be used for DU fractures with a fractured or displaced ulnar styloid in order to apply compression on the fracture site",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423223/images/34f48d90-2d2f-4a59-b496-202b7a4bf3e1_screenshot_2025-03-28_at_4.32.34_pm.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The DU Base Plate may be used for DU neck fractures and neck fractures that are extending into the shaft of the ulna",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423223/images/9a0d78db-5e26-4e5a-a8cc-fa95b7d7b215_screenshot_2025-03-28_at_4.32.37_pm.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approach",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "DU Hook Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "A longitudinal incision is made over the palpable ulna",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Expose the distal ulna in the region between the tendons of the flexor carpi ulnaris and extensor carpi ulnaris toward the ulnar styloid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Fracture fragments can be visualizedand reduced. The fractured ulna styloid should be reduced and temporarily stabilized with a K-wire",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "DU Base Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "A longitudinal incision is made over the palpable ulna",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Expose the distal ulna in the region between the tendons of the flexor carpi ulnaris and extensor carpi ulnaris toward the ulnar styloid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Fracture fragments can be visualized and reduced",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "DU Hook Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The plate is slipped over the K-wire and placed along the medial aspect of the ulna, ensuring the distal hook is secured around the ulnar styloid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Plate placement can be adjusted by sliding the plate along the K-wire through the K-wire slot",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "DU Base Plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Place the plate on the medial aspect of the ulna",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Temporary plate fixation can be achieved by inserting a K-wire through the proximal K-wire hole or by placing an olive-stop K-wire through two of the screw holes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Specific Plates",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Distal Ulna Hook Plate",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423223/images/e3384dff-56d4-43b1-bafa-313ee9e7b027_screenshot_2025-03-27_at_9.19.08_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "SOMA designed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "1.5mm thickness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Distal hook allows for fragment reduction by K-wire prior to plate fixation and plate can be slid over K-wire for final reduction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Distal Ulna Base Plate",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423223/images/a1c0ff69-49b7-4f3d-98e1-e49e0b637354_screenshot_2025-03-27_at_9.19.17_am.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "SOMA designed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "1.7mm thickness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Distal screw cluster offers more fixation options in a narrow footprint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Locking screws are laser marked with a ‘dot’ and ‘ring’ marking on the screw head to differentiate them from non-locking screws",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Locking and Non-Locking screws can be used in any round hole",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Allows for ±15 degrees of angulation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The 2.0mm drill guide for T8 Screws facilitates drilling a 2.0mm pilot hole for a 2.4 or 2.7mm T8 screw or a 2.0mm peg centrically for locking or non-locking screws",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
